   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 509 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law relating\nto authorizing the imposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Port\nChester, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6700",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6700-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 509 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6700\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 509 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law\nrelating to authorizing the imposition of an occupancy tax in the\nvillage of Port Chester, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nTo extend the authority of the village of Port Chester to impose a room\noccupancy tax not to exceed 3%.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. This bill extends the current village of Port Chester occu-\npancy tax for another two years until December 31, 2027.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill extends the current Village of Port Chester occupancy tax.\nThe Village of Port Chester anticipates using this revenue as an alter-\nnative to raising property taxes or additional borrowing.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: S8041/A9116; L 2022, ch.411\n\n2019: S5080/A6553; L 2019, ch.709\n\n2016: S7152/A9694; L 2016, ch.509\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
